## Context
- IVic.sol#L4-L6
- VaultV2.sol#L198-L202
- IManualVic.sol#L25

## Description
Currently, there is only one implementation of the IVic, i.e., IManualVic. One might assume that IVic implementations are only connected to one unique vault during their lifetime.

## Recommendation
If the above assumption is true, then one can move up the definition of `vault()` from `IManualVic` to `IVic` and also add a check in `setVic(...)` to make sure that the `newVic` added points back to the same vault. If an IVic could potentially be connected to multiple vaults, this possibility should at least be documented.

